  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 310 AM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nAn upper level shortwave trough will move northeast across the\nsouthern Plains on Friday then across the area on Saturday into\nSunday. Much of the day will be dry across the area on Friday with\nthe upper level energy remaining to the southwest of the area.\nAs the upper level trough approaches the area scattered showers\nand maybe a few rumbles of thunder will develop Friday night\ninto Saturday morning. This rainfall will likely be light in\nnature. As additional upper level energy moves through the area\non Saturday into early Sunday, bands of showers and maybe few \nthunderstorms will be possible. There will be dry periods on \nSaturday and rainfall amounts may be light  generally rainfall \nfrom a few tenth of an inch to one half inch of rainfall. There \ncould be locally heavy amounts with any thunderstorms that can \ndevelop. No severe weather or flooding is expected this weekend.\n\nThe ensemble model members then show an upper level low moving\ntowards the region early next week. The models differ on the\nexact track, structure, and timing of the system from run to \nrun and with each other. Therefore, confidence on the timing is\nstill low for the area. Better lift will occur with this system\nwhich could result in better widespread rainfall amounts, but \nthe timing and rainfall amounts and impacts will be dependent on\nthe track and structure of the system.\n\nHighs in the 70s are expected this weekend into Monday with \nhighs in the 60s by the middle of next week.",
